      "hints": [
        "Coordinates: $P(t, 5t)$ and $Q(t, 9t-t^3)$.",
        "$PQ = (9t - t^3) - 5t = 4t - t^3$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Determine the $y$-coordinates of points $P$ on $y = 5x$ and $Q$ on $y = x(9 - x^2)$ at $x = t$:\n$$y_P = 5t, \\quad y_Q = t(9 - t^2) = 9t - t^3$$",
        "Subtract the $y$-coordinates to find the vertical length $PQ$:\n$$PQ = y_Q - y_P = (9t - t^3) - 5t = 4t - t^3$$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_w18_12_q3_ii",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p1_t_differentiation",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p1_t_differentiation_m06_l01"
      },
      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $PQ$: $\\frac{d(PQ)}{dt} = 4 - 3t^2 = 0 \\implies t = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$.",
        "Evaluate $PQ = 4(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}) - \\frac{8}{3\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{16\\sqrt{3}}{9} \\approx 3.08$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $PQ = 4t - t^3$ with respect to $t$ and set to zero:\n$$\\frac{d(PQ)}{dt} = 4 - 3t^2 = 0 \\implies 3t^2 = 4 \\implies t = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$$",
        "Substitute $t = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ into the expression for $PQ$:\n$$PQ_{\\max} = 4\\left(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right) - \\left(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)^3 = \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}} - \\frac{8}{3\\sqrt{3}}$$",
        "Simplify the exact maximum length:\n$$PQ_{\\max} = \\frac{24 - 8}{3\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{16}{3\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{16\\sqrt{3}}{9} \\quad (\\text{or } \\approx 3.08)$$"
      ]
    }
  ]
